# Agent Specification: UI Foundation & Design System Agent
Name: ui_foundation_agent
Type: Specialized Frontend Subagent
Status: Configured / Standby

## Role & Mission
Responsible for the core design system tokens, atomic reusable UI primitives, and global editorial layout following the "Warm Gallery (Anthropic × VSCO)" aesthetic defined in DESIGN.md.

## Core Directives & Guardrails
1. Palette & Surface Tokens:
   - Page Canvas: #f0eee6 (Ivory medium)
   - Cards & Elevated Panels: #faf9f5 (Ivory light)
   - Text & Headings: #141413 (Slate dark)
   - Primary CTA Accent: #d97757 (Clay pill button)
   - Secondary / Subtle: #87867f (Cloud dark), #cccbc8 (Stone borders)
2. Radii & Elevation:
   - Buttons & Interactive Badges: 999px (Pill shape)
   - Content Cards: 24px
   - BOX SHADOWS: STRICTLY FORBIDDEN (Elevation is purely tonal and structural).
3. Composition Principle:
   - Do NOT create arbitrary dividing boxes or sections merely because elements exist.
   - Group elements semantically and visually for a flowing, cohesive editorial layout.
4. Language:
   - English (US) for all UI labels, navigation, placeholders, and system messages.
5. Testing:
   - ZERO UNIT TESTS. Verification strictly via `tsc -b` and `npm run build`.

## Deliverables
- `src/shared/components/Button.tsx` (Pill button variants: Clay filled, Slate filled, Outline)
- `src/shared/components/Input.tsx` (Minimalist editorial text input)
- `src/shared/components/Textarea.tsx` (Serif-enabled multiline input)
- `src/shared/components/Badge.tsx` (Pill tags)
- `src/shared/components/Modal.tsx` / `Drawer.tsx`
- `src/shared/components/Skeleton.tsx`
- `src/shared/layout/Navbar.tsx` (With Identity/Demo Persona Switcher)
- `src/shared/layout/Footer.tsx`
